course: dictionary
lesson: 2878
title: Doom and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Doom is a dark word. Its main meaning is death, ruin or a terrible fate that cannot be avoided. «The plan was doomed from the start» uses it as a verb: the plan was certain to fail.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Impending doom» and «a sense of doom» sound frightening, so doom means something bad that is coming. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The plan was certain to fail from the start" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Doom also shows up in everyday talk. «Doom and gloom» means a feeling that everything will go wrong, like grumbling about the weather or a test. Doomscrolling means reading lots of bad news online. The sentence tells you which meaning you are reading.
explain: Some doom words are old or special. In 1086 the Domesday Book counted England's land, people and animals for taxes, and there doom meant judgement, because the records were final. It is not about the end of the world, so check the sentence before you panic.
fact: Doom most often means a terrible fate that cannot be avoided.
fact: «The plan was doomed from the start» means the plan was certain to fail.
fact: «Doom and gloom» means a feeling that everything will go wrong.
fact: The Domesday Book was an old English survey from 1086, not a book about the end of the world.
fact: Slang: «it's giving doom» (Gen Alpha) means it feels like doom.
exercise: «The plan was doomed from the start.» What does doomed mean here? | Full of fun and surprises | *Certain to fail | Finished early and well | Written down on paper
exercise: Maya says, «It's giving doom», about a sad film. What does she mean? | *It feels like doom | It is very funny | It is a big wooden door | It is giving away free tickets
exercise: Which phrase means a feeling that everything will go wrong? | Stars and stripes | *Doom and gloom | Rain and sunshine | Bread and butter
test: «The villain plotted doom for the whole town.» What does doom most likely mean here? | *Terrible ruin | A happy party | A tasty cake | A new pair of shoes
test: In 1086 the Domesday Book counted England's land for taxes. What did doom mean then? | *Judgement, because the records were final | A loud noise | A happy ending | Dark clouds in the sky
exam: Ella says, «Doomscrolling all night made me sad.» What is doomscrolling? | Drawing scrolls in a castle | Dancing in the dark | Sleeping with the lights on | *Reading lots of bad news online
